{"id":"glu_cklicherweise","lemma":"glücklicherweise","pos":"adv","rank":4063,"glosses":["fortunately; luckily"],"ipa":"/ˈɡlʏklɪçɐˌvaɪ̯zə/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/9/9c/De-gl%C3%BCcklicherweise.ogg/De-gl%C3%BCcklicherweise.ogg.mp3","examples":[{"text":"Glücklicherweise wurde niemand verletzt.","en":"Fortunately, no one was hurt.","words":[null,{"g":"to become","l":"werden"},{"g":"nobody, no one"},{"g":"hurt, injured"}]},{"text":"Glücklicherweise war es diese Woche warm.","en":"Luckily, it was warm this week.","words":[null,{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"it"},{"g":"this one, this","l":"dieser"},{"g":"week"},{"g":"warm"}]},{"text":"Glücklicherweise war das Wetter schön.","en":"Fortunately, the weather was good.","words":[null,{"g":"was","l":"sein"},{"g":"the / that"},{"g":"weather"},{"g":"well, beautifully"}]},{"text":"Glücklicherweise habe ich dich zum Reden.","en":"Fortunately, I've got you to talk to.","words":[null,{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"you","l":"du"},{"g":"to the"},{"g":"to talk"}]},{"text":"Glücklicherweise habe ich meine Schlüssel gefunden.","en":"Luckily, I found my keys.","words":[null,{"g":"have","l":"haben"},{"g":"I"},{"g":"my","l":"mein"},{"g":"a key"},{"g":"found, located"}]}]}